-- title:
--   Points over algebraically closed π-nilpotent 𝒪-algebras
-- statement:
--   Let $r$ be a prime, let $\mathcal{O}$ be a commutative domain of characteristic zero which is a discrete valuation ring, let $\pi \in \mathcal{O}$ be irreducible, assume the quotient $\mathcal{O}/(\pi)$ has exactly $r$ elements and that $(r) = (\pi)$ as ideals of $\mathcal{O}$; let $K_0$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a fraction field of $\mathcal{O}$. Let $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ be a commutative domain of characteristic zero and an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra such that the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ in $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ is maximal and every element of $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ satisfies some monic polynomial over $\mathcal{O}$ whose value at that element lies in that ideal. Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field and an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent. The conclusion is twofold: the set of $\mathcal{O}$-algebra homomorphisms $O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to k$ is non-empty, and the value at $k$ of the functor `Omega` is non-empty, i.e. there exists a Deligne datum over $k$ for $\pi$ relative to $K_0$: an assignment to each full $\mathcal{O}$-lattice $M$ in $K_0^2$ of a $k$-submodule of $k \otimes_{\mathcal{O}} M$ with invertible quotient, compatible with lattice inclusions and with homothety by $K_0^\times$, and satisfying the non-degeneracy condition at every prime ideal of $k$.
--
--   This is the non-emptiness input for the Čerednik–Drinfeld comparison: both sides of the uniformisation have points over every algebraically closed test field in which $\pi$ is nilpotent, the left-hand statement providing the $\mathcal{O}$-point of the unramified coefficient ring used to rigidify the comparison. It is invoked in the verification that the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation identifies the relevant fine moduli problems for quaternionic Shimura curves.
